      "writtenOn": "2020-01-13T21:12:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is this line supposed to do?\n\nAre you trying to find out if there would be a change of the SOV register?\n\nI think that mask^it8801_gpio_sov[port] will give you the value of the sov as if you toggled the pin, not sure why you have that as your if condition, it\u0027s very likely it\u0027s always nonzero.\n\nI think you want something like this (but i haven\u0027t tried it, you should)\n\nfuture_register_value \u003d (it8801_gpio_sov[port] \u0026 (~mask)) | (mask * value) // original register with anything at mask cleared, then ored with our mask depending on if value is set\nif (future_register_value !\u003d it8801_gpio_sov[port]) {\n    it8801_gpio_sov[port] \u003d future_register_value;\n    rv \u003d it8801_write(IT8801_REG_GPIO_SOVR(port), it8801_gpio_sov[port]);\n}\n\nor\n\nif (!!(it8801_gpio_sov[port] \u0026 mask) ^ value) // is the bit at mask different than our value\n// and keep the rest of your code",
      "range": {
