      "writtenOn": "2020-01-13T21:12:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This might be wrong too again.\n\nAnd this will not prevent the it8801_write(IT8801_REG_GPIO_SOVR from running when the SOVR didn\u0027t change either. Not to mention that the _CR doesn\u0027t have a cache either so there\u0027s extra writes there too.\n\nBy implementing caching here the idea would be that a second consecutive call to it8801_ioex_set_flags_by_mask with the same arguments will not cause any i2c transactions to go out. Right now you still have the exact same amount of i2c transactions.\n\nRegardless, i don\u0027t know how necessary caching is to it8801_ioex_set_flags_by_mask, it might not be an important enough function to worry about it.\n\nMy main concern with caching was for the set_level in keyboard_raw_drive_column, since that reduces i2c transactions by half.",
